From e982d98fe9bfb3cfd3c17811ff55e09af82cb242 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 06:09:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: emit RB_DEPTH_INFO in sysmem prep so depth
 buffer is correctly configured

fd2_emit_sysmem_prep() emits RB_SURFACE_INFO + RB_COLOR_INFO + scissor for
the sysmem render path, but never emits RB_DEPTH_INFO. So in sysmem mode the
depth register is left at the GPU power-on default (DEPTHX_16, BASE=0).
Depth-test then reads garbage at iova 0 and geometry gets randomly z-rejected,
producing visible corruption.

This is why every glmark2 scene with a depth buffer fails --validate under
FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem on A22X (build:use-vbo=false, shading:blinn-phong-inf,
bump:bump-render=normals all Failure) while the SAME scenes pass cleanly
under GMEM -- where the per-tile RB_DEPTH_INFO emit in fd2_emit_tile_renderprep
(fd2_gmem.c:651-659) correctly sets DEPTHX_24_8 + DEPTH_BASE=gmem_zsbuf_offset.

Compared by RD-dump capture (memory/project_a220_blur_hang_cmdstream_analysis
for the method): the build:use-vbo=false sysmem submit01 has the depth
register left at the prior clear-IB's DEPTHX_16+BASE=0 leftover; under GMEM
the same scene emits DEPTHX_24_8+BASE=0x30000 per tile. App-visible result:
random missing geometry / depth-flicker in sysmem mode.

This is the root cause of the e03abba3356 'force sysmem on A22X' revert --
that experiment was correct in spirit (matches what KGSL ships, bins=0 for
all observed workloads per memory/reference_kgsl_vs_freedreno_heavy_scene)
but exposed this missing depth-info emit. With this fix, force-sysmem
becomes a viable path.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
index 20f38ce54a7..d1aef734687 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
@@ -507,6 +507,28 @@ fd2_emit_sysmem_prep(struct fd_batch *batch)
                 A2XX_RB_COLOR_INFO_FORMAT(fd2_pipe2color(psurf->format)),
              0);
 
+   /* Emit RB_DEPTH_INFO with the depth buffer's iova + format. Without this,
+    * the depth register is left at default DEPTHX_16+BASE=0, depth-test reads
+    * garbage at iova 0, and geometry gets randomly z-rejected -> visible
+    * corruption (--validate fails on every scene with a depth buffer in
+    * sysmem mode, while the SAME scenes pass under GMEM where the per-tile
+    * RB_DEPTH_INFO emit in fd2_emit_tile_renderprep configures the depth
+    * correctly). GMEM-side depth-info emit at line ~656 was always present;
+    * the sysmem-side equivalent was missing.
+    */
+   if (pfb->zsbuf.texture) {
+      struct pipe_surface *zsurf = &pfb->zsbuf;
+      struct fd_resource *zrsc = fd_resource(zsurf->texture);
+      uint32_t zoffset =
+         fd_resource_offset(zrsc, zsurf->level, zsurf->first_layer);
+
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
+      OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_RB_DEPTH_INFO));
+      OUT_RELOC(ring, zrsc->bo, zoffset,
+                A2XX_RB_DEPTH_INFO_DEPTH_FORMAT(fd_pipe2depth(zsurf->format)),
+                0);
+   }
+
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 3);
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_PA_SC_SCREEN_SCISSOR_TL));
    OUT_RING(ring, A2XX_PA_SC_SCREEN_SCISSOR_TL_WINDOW_OFFSET_DISABLE);
-- 
